## SMS setup (Twilio)

1. Buy a Twilio phone number.
2. In the Twilio console → Phone Number → "A message comes in": HTTP POST to
   `https://<your-domain>/sms/incoming`.
3. Set `TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID`, `TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN` in env. If the token is
   unset, **all inbound SMS is rejected** (fail closed — verified signature
   is mandatory).

Text `JOIN <username> <password>` from your phone to link the number to your
web account (so the bot remembers you on both channels). `UNLINK` detaches.

## Admin review queue

Guarded by `X-Admin-Key: $ADMIN_API_KEY` header:

- `GET /admin/candidates` — pending leads from the growth agent
- `POST /admin/candidates/{id}/approve` — promotes the candidate into a verified
  `Resource` (it becomes user-visible here, not before)
- `POST /admin/candidates/{id}/reject`
- `POST /admin/growth/run` — kick the growth agent manually

## API surface

| Endpoint | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `POST /api/auth/register` | Create account (returns JWT) |
| `POST /api/auth/login` | Frontend-argoru JWT |
| `POST /api/auth/recover/start` \| `/finish` | Question-based password reset |
| `POST /api/chat` | Web chat (auth optional; anon = no memory) |
| `POST /api/chat/image` | Web chat with a photo (JSON: `image_base64`, `media_type`) |
| `GET /api/resources` | Verified directory (`?city=&service_type=`) |
| `GET /api/resources/context?query=` | Debug: what RAG would inject |
| `POST /sms/incoming` | Twilio webhook (signature-validated) |

